 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Router() starts with no routes. A path is \"/\" (no segments) or \"/\" followed by segments joined with \"/\"; a pattern has the same form but any segment may be \"*\". addRoute(pattern, handler) registers pattern with handler, replacing the handler of an identical earlier pattern. callRoute(path) considers the registered patterns with as many segments as path whose every non-\"*\" segment equals the path segment at the same position; it returns the handler of the one with the fewest \"*\" segments, breaking ties by preferring a literal segment over \"*\" at the leftmost position where two candidates differ; it returns \"\" when no pattern matches. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk17-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
